1
00:00:03,865 --> 00:00:06,327
The Lives of Prophets Part 1;

2
00:00:06,778 --> 00:00:10,394
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

3
00:00:10,576 --> 00:00:14,628
In sha Allah Ho Tala(إن شاء الله تعالى), we'll talk tonight about Khateeb Ul Ambiyaa(خطيب الأنبِيَاء)

4
00:00:16,176 --> 00:00:20,381
the Speaker of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), the orator of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

5
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:23,379
This Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

6
00:00:23,409 --> 00:00:26,958
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given him eloquence in speech.

7
00:00:28,295 --> 00:00:34,366
He had beautiful words of wisdom and advice, Naseeha(نَصيحة) that he delivered to his people.

8
00:00:36,185 --> 00:00:43,700
His story is short but it is full of meanings for all of us

9
00:00:43,915 --> 00:00:51,676
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not mention to us the story of any Nabi(نَبِي), except because there are lessons for us to learn.

10
00:00:53,208 --> 00:00:56,686
This Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is Syedina(سيدنا) Shoaib عليه السّلام.

11
00:00:57,488 --> 00:01:07,062
Syedina(سَيِّدِنَا) Shoaib عليه السلام, we do not know exactly where he lies in terms of the chronological order.

12
00:01:09,858 --> 00:01:13,014
He is from the descendants of Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

13
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:16,953
There are some scholars who say

14
00:01:18,691 --> 00:01:25,998
that Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) is the one, whom Qur'an talks about that Musa(موسى) married his daughter

15
00:01:28,244 --> 00:01:31,601
but Qur'an does not specifically stated, it was Shoaib(شُعَيب).

16
00:01:32,306 --> 00:01:39,144
It just says that Musa(موسى) went to Madyan(مدين) and he got married, to his wife in Madyan(مدين).

17
00:01:40,381 --> 00:01:46,337
So some of the Ulama(علماء) concluded that it might be Shoaib(شُعَيب) because Shoaib(شُعَيب) was the Nabi(نَبِي) of Madyan(مدين).

18
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:54,464
So that's why I'll talk about Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) tonight after Saydina Ibrahim(سيِدنَااِبْراهِيْم) being from the descendants of Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

19
00:01:54,845 --> 00:01:59,665
but we don't know where exactly it comes in terms of the time order, but that's not a problem.

20
00:01:59,948 --> 00:02:06,898
It wouldn't do us any benefit to know the timeline of these events

21
00:02:07,445 --> 00:02:14,183
and it won't do us any harm not to know when it happened because the essence of the lessons are there.

22
00:02:14,918 --> 00:02:20,058
Whether it happened long time before Musa(موسى) or it happened in the time Musa(موسى) it doesn't make a difference

23
00:02:21,757 --> 00:02:27,581
and Syedina(سَيِّدِنَا) Shoaib عليه السلام made Da'wah(دعوة) to his people in Madyan(مدين).

24
00:02:28,763 --> 00:02:32,311
Madyan(مدين) is the town, the area.

25
00:02:33,613 --> 00:02:34,741
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

26
00:02:34,801 --> 00:02:42,126
وَإِلىٰ مَديَنَ أَخاهُم شُعَيبًا ۚ

27
00:02:42,178 --> 00:02:46,108
And to the people of Madyan(مدين), their brother Shoaib(شُعَيب).

28
00:02:47,028 --> 00:02:49,140
What does brother here mean?

29
00:02:49,925 --> 00:02:54,506
It means he is part of them, he's from those people.

30
00:02:57,155 --> 00:03:01,079
But in another Ayah(آية), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

31
00:03:01,145 --> 00:03:06,169
كَذَّبَ أَصْحَٰبُ لْـَٔيْكَةِ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ۝إِذ قالَ لَهُم شُعَيبٌ

32
00:03:07,747 --> 00:03:15,633
The people of the Aikah(لْـَٔيْكَةِ) disbelieved in the messengers, when Shoaib(شُعَيب) was sent to them.

33
00:03:16,406 --> 00:03:18,518
Over here in this Ayah(آية) it didn't say Brother,

34
00:03:19,042 --> 00:03:22,582
even though in Surat-Ash'Shuara(سورة الشعراء) and this is from Surat-Ash'Shuara(سورة الشعراء)

35
00:03:23,925 --> 00:03:25,666
when it talks about Aad(عاد) it says;

36
00:03:25,696 --> 00:03:26,786
  أخاهم هودَا

37
00:03:26,944 --> 00:03:27,968
their brother Hud(هود),

38
00:03:28,325 --> 00:03:30,127
when it talks about Thamud(ثمود) it says;

39
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:31,206
 أخاهم صالح

40
00:03:31,236 --> 00:03:32,560
there brother Saleh(صالح),

41
00:03:32,766 --> 00:03:35,869
when it talks about Lut(لوط),

42
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:37,385
 أخاهم لوط

43
00:03:37,679 --> 00:03:38,766
brother Lut(لوط)

44
00:03:39,313 --> 00:03:42,742
but it didn't say their brother Shoaib(شُعَيب).

45
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,382
Why?

46
00:03:45,289 --> 00:03:46,928
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says;

47
00:03:47,984 --> 00:03:52,087
Because in that Ayah(آية) Allah was saying the people of Aikah(لْـَٔيْكَةِ).

48
00:03:52,428 --> 00:03:55,842
Aikah(لْـَٔيْكَةِ) is a large tree, which they used to worship.

49
00:03:57,191 --> 00:03:59,167
So Allah said: The people of Aikah(لْـَٔيْكَةِ)

50
00:03:59,746 --> 00:04:07,196
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not want to attribute Brotherhood to the people of Aikah(لْـَٔيْكَةِ)

51
00:04:08,338 --> 00:04:11,344
because Aikah(لْـَٔيْكَةِ) is a God that is taken besides Allah.

52
00:04:11,519 --> 00:04:14,673
So Allah said: Shoaib(شُعَيب) without saying their brother,

53
00:04:14,891 --> 00:04:16,128
but when Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

54
00:04:16,158 --> 00:04:17,237
 إلى مدين

55
00:04:18,317 --> 00:04:22,055
when we sent to Madyan(مدين), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said: Their brother, Shoaib(شُعَيب)

56
00:04:22,968 --> 00:04:26,685
and this is a small note in terms of the difference in the Ayaat(آيات).

57
00:04:27,593 --> 00:04:52,473
قالَ يا قَومِ اعبُدُوا اللَّهَ ما لَكُم مِن إِلٰهٍ غَيرُهُ ۖ قَد جاءَتكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِن رَبِّكُم ۖ

58
00:04:52,503 --> 00:04:56,857
Worship Allah you have no other God but Him.

59
00:04:58,206 --> 00:05:00,515
قَد جاءَتكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِن رَبِّكُم ۖ

60
00:05:01,745 --> 00:05:04,570
You have a clear sign from Allah.

61
00:05:04,944 --> 00:05:20,093
فَأَوفُوا الكَيلَ وَالميزانَ وَلا تَبخَسُوا النّاسَ أَشياءَهُم

62
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:25,228
So give full measure and full weight and wrong not men in their things.

63
00:05:27,022 --> 00:05:33,997
Madyan(مَدْيَن) was on the trade route of Hijaz(حجاز) and Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

64
00:05:36,404 --> 00:05:41,967
It was a financial centre and the people of Madyan(مَدْيَن) were rich.

65
00:05:42,983 --> 00:05:47,141
Their job was their work, or their trade was business.

66
00:05:48,094 --> 00:05:50,943
But they were unfair in their business dealings.

67
00:05:51,671 --> 00:05:55,314
And they used to cheat and they would not give full measure.

68
00:05:55,981 --> 00:05:58,306
Syedina(سَيِّدِنَا) Shoaib عليه السلام said;

69
00:05:58,425 --> 00:06:00,235
فَأَوفُوا الكَيلَ وَالميزانَ

70
00:06:00,473 --> 00:06:03,140
Give full measure and full weight,

71
00:06:03,819 --> 00:06:05,153
وَلا تُفسِدوا فِي الأَرضِ

72
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:08,288
And do not cause corruption in the land.

73
00:06:10,129 --> 00:06:14,159
The people of Shoaib(شُعَيب) even though they were wealthy,

74
00:06:16,128 --> 00:06:21,675
they were still cheating thinking that this is their source of Rizq(رزق)

75
00:06:22,604 --> 00:06:25,525
and that is Tadfeef Al-Mizan(تدفيف الميزان)

76
00:06:26,366 --> 00:06:30,511
so you would put a weight and tell the person this is one pound but it's not it's less than that.

77
00:06:31,487 --> 00:06:34,043
And they would also cheat in transactions.

78
00:06:35,694 --> 00:06:42,151
We find that every Nabi(نَبِي) came with the same message and that is;

79
00:06:42,181 --> 00:06:43,183
لا اله إلَّا الله

80
00:06:43,429 --> 00:06:44,889
There is no God but Allah

81
00:06:46,482 --> 00:06:53,490
but then the details of the message were different according to the situation of the people.

82
00:06:55,090 --> 00:07:03,285
Last night when we talked about the people of Lut(لوط), their disease and illness was their lust.

83
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,690
So we find that Lut(لوط) was dealing with that problem.

84
00:07:10,277 --> 00:07:16,422
The people of Madyan(مَدْيَن) their problem was in their business transactions, in their Muamalat(معاملات),

85
00:07:16,882 --> 00:07:22,567
they were cheating when it comes to money; they did not follow the law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

86
00:07:23,164 --> 00:07:26,043
And with the people of Aad(عاد) they had certain diseases

87
00:07:26,073 --> 00:07:28,393
with the people of Thamood(ثمود) they had certain diseases

88
00:07:28,716 --> 00:07:35,303
with Musa(موسى) and the story of Musa عليه السّلام we find that he was dealing with the dictatorship

89
00:07:35,363 --> 00:07:43,977
and the oppression of Firaun(فرعون) on one side, and then he was dealing with the problems of his own Ummah(امة),

90
00:07:44,007 --> 00:07:47,307
the Muslims of that time Banu Israel(بنواسرائيل) on the other hand.

91
00:07:49,185 --> 00:07:52,652
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى mentions to us these stories in Qur'an

92
00:07:52,875 --> 00:07:59,082
because we are going to need every one of them because we are going to run into similar situations.

93
00:08:00,371 --> 00:08:03,391
That's why Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is mentioning the stories in Qur'an.

94
00:08:04,431 --> 00:08:09,084
So we are going to deal with problems similar to the problems that Lut(لوط) faced

95
00:08:10,370 --> 00:08:15,897
and these are the lust and the sexual desire put in places where it shouldn't be.

96
00:08:17,519 --> 00:08:22,795
We are going to run into situations where people are cheating in business.

97
00:08:23,914 --> 00:08:29,637
We are going to run into situations of oppressive governments like Firaun(فرعون).

98
00:08:30,309 --> 00:08:39,259
We are going to run into the problem of dealing with our own Muslim brothers, who are not keeping the rule of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

99
00:08:39,406 --> 00:08:42,390
just like Musa(موسى) was dealing with Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

100
00:08:43,707 --> 00:08:48,846
and we are going to run into problems similar to every other story of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) mentioned  in Qur'an.

101
00:08:49,929 --> 00:08:57,495
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is mentioning for us, these stories for us to learn the lessons of how to deal with these particular situations.

102
00:09:00,201 --> 00:09:08,623
The issue of business is a very, very important part of religion.

103
00:09:09,078 --> 00:09:12,043
That we are taking very, very, very lightly

104
00:09:13,138 --> 00:09:22,681
because we find that there are some people who are the best in terms of their attendance to Salah(صلاة)

105
00:09:23,298 --> 00:09:26,550
and their attachment to the Faraid(فرائض) of Islam

106
00:09:27,145 --> 00:09:33,277
and their application to many of the Sunnan(سنن) of Rasool Allah ﷺ they are the best in that

107
00:09:33,896 --> 00:09:39,912
and on the other side they're the best in cheating, and Tadfeef Al-Mizan(تدفيف الميزان) and wronging others in business.

108
00:09:40,735 --> 00:09:44,858
How could these two sides exist in the same person?

109
00:09:45,930 --> 00:09:50,335
In the Masjid(مسجد), we could be in that state of devotion to worship,

110
00:09:50,581 --> 00:09:57,657
and just as we cross our feet outside of the door of the Masjid(مسجد), a completely different personality.

111
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:06,251
Inside the Masjid(مسجد) the Lord is Allah outside the Masjid(مسجد) the Lord is the dollar.

112
00:10:07,503 --> 00:10:13,582
Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) was dealing with this problem and then we will find something interesting.

113
00:10:13,805 --> 00:10:19,632
The response of his people was similar to the response of the people you will speak to today,

114
00:10:19,735 --> 00:10:23,489
when they are not keeping the right business transaction, so we'll get into that.

115
00:10:25,751 --> 00:10:31,780
They also used to tax anybody who's passing through.

116
00:10:32,606 --> 00:10:40,979
As-Sidi(ألسِّدِّي), one of the Mufassireen(مفسرين), he says these are the first people to start taxation and tariffs, Customs.

117
00:10:41,114 --> 00:10:44,376
Whenever somebody is passing through Madyan(مَدْيَن), you have to pay customs.

118
00:10:45,564 --> 00:10:47,818
As-Sidi(ألسِّدِّي) says these are the first people to start that

119
00:10:47,945 --> 00:10:53,565
before you would travel in and out and nobody would tax you and take from you customs.

120
00:10:53,905 --> 00:10:56,670
Anybody who's passing going to Al-Hijaz(حجاز)

121
00:10:56,954 --> 00:10:59,088
going from Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) to Hijaz(حجاز) has to pay a tax

122
00:10:59,223 --> 00:11:02,032
if you're going from al Hijaz(حجاز) to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام), you have to pay them a tax.

123
00:11:02,461 --> 00:11:09,318
In addition to that, they would rob sometimes some of these caravans that are going on the way

124
00:11:10,005 --> 00:11:15,449
and they would also prevent the people from becoming Muslim and listening to the message of Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب),

125
00:11:15,846 --> 00:11:17,830
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

126
00:11:18,211 --> 00:11:35,182
وَيا قَومِ أَوفُوا المِكيالَ وَالميزانَ بِالقِسطِ ۖ وَلا تَبخَسُوا النّاسَ أَشياءَهُم وَلا تَعثَوا فِي الأَرضِ مُفسِدينَ۝

127
00:11:36,467 --> 00:11:45,333
بَقِيَّتُ اللَّهِ خَيرٌ لَكُم إِن كُنتُم مُؤمِنينَ ۚ

128
00:11:45,411 --> 00:11:52,642
And O my people give full measure and weigh in injustice and reduce not the things that are due to the people

129
00:11:52,927 --> 00:11:56,388
and do not commit mischief in the land causing corruption;

130
00:11:56,697 --> 00:12:00,836
that which is left by Allah for you is better for you.

131
00:12:01,498 --> 00:12:06,090
Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) is telling them: Do not cheat and give full measure.

132
00:12:07,621 --> 00:12:10,085
He is telling them give full measure

133
00:12:11,299 --> 00:12:19,663
and then give the Zaka'at(زكوة) and give the Sadaqah(صدقة) and what will remain of that is better for you.

134
00:12:21,856 --> 00:12:27,310
Because people without Eeman(ايمان) tend to think that

135
00:12:28,064 --> 00:12:31,349
if I cheat I will be able to make more money.

136
00:12:32,110 --> 00:12:35,983
That's the logic that we think with, when we don't have Eeman(ايمان).

137
00:12:37,041 --> 00:12:39,236
Shoaib(شُعَيب) was telling them: No! That's wrong.

138
00:12:39,998 --> 00:12:44,494
When you cheat and you make more money, you're not really making more money; you are losing.

139
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:50,185
If you give full measure you give the people what is due to them

140
00:12:50,701 --> 00:12:55,510
and then you give out for your money the obligations that you have towards the poor.

141
00:12:56,155 --> 00:13:01,450
What will remain to you even though it seems less, but it is better for you.

142
00:13:02,149 --> 00:13:05,390
Then the bigger amount that you can make through cheating.

143
00:13:05,483 --> 00:13:07,489
بَقِيَّتُ اللَّهِ خَيرٌ لَكُم

144
00:13:07,727 --> 00:13:10,759
What will remain for you is better for you

145
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:18,474
and we find that this is approved through Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an and through Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

146
00:13:19,645 --> 00:13:21,188
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

147
00:13:21,450 --> 00:13:22,498
يَمْحَقُ اللّهُ الْرِّبَا

148
00:13:22,558 --> 00:13:25,627
Riba(رباء) interest is one of the things that increases your money.

149
00:13:26,670 --> 00:13:31,146
If you are getting interest, you're taking interest; you're making more money,

150
00:13:31,281 --> 00:13:32,413
but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

151
00:13:32,443 --> 00:13:34,926
يَمْحَقُ اللّهُ الْرِّبَا وَيُرْبِي الصَّدَقَاتِ

152
00:13:35,568 --> 00:13:36,394
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

153
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:40,188
when you're dealing with interest, this is talking about the one who's taking interest.

154
00:13:40,394 --> 00:13:45,852
When you take interest you're making more money; when you're giving Sadaqah(صدقة) you're losing money

155
00:13:46,953 --> 00:13:47,960
but the Ayah(آية) says;

156
00:13:48,024 --> 00:13:50,135
يَمْحَقُ اللّهُ الْرِّبَا وَيُرْبِي الصَّدَقَاتِ

157
00:13:50,358 --> 00:13:53,578
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى destroys and decreases interest

158
00:13:53,935 --> 00:13:58,252
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى increases and expands Sadaqah(صدقة); charity.

159
00:13:58,673 --> 00:14:01,509
It's the exact opposite of what we think.

160
00:14:03,761 --> 00:14:04,340
Why?

161
00:14:04,370 --> 00:14:09,758
Because we're missing a very, very important element in wealth and that is the issue of Barakah(بركة).

162
00:14:11,179 --> 00:14:16,853
We think always in terms of numbers, exact numbers $200 is more than 100.

163
00:14:17,823 --> 00:14:21,752
We are not including in the calculation, the concept of Barakah(بركة).

164
00:14:23,077 --> 00:14:26,627
Barakah(بركة) is a secret that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى puts in the money.

165
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:33,938
So, the $100 could not only be more than 200, it could be more than 1000

166
00:14:34,383 --> 00:14:37,994
because it has that secret element in it; called Barakah(بركة), blessing.

167
00:14:39,298 --> 00:14:43,584
So $1 that has Barakah(بركة) could go a long way

168
00:14:44,092 --> 00:14:47,932
and $1 that does not have Barakah(بركة) could cause you  destruction.

169
00:14:50,662 --> 00:14:52,321
And we see that a lot;

170
00:14:53,345 --> 00:14:57,220
you see that some people, they're living off a small amount of money,

171
00:14:57,250 --> 00:15:01,535
but they're having a very blessed and pleasant life, they're happy and they are content from an inside.

172
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:06,287
And you see that somebody else has a lot, but they're living a life of misery.

173
00:15:07,461 --> 00:15:07,830
Why?

174
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:09,295
Because Barakah(بركة) is missing.

175
00:15:10,057 --> 00:15:11,989
So Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) is telling his people,

176
00:15:12,215 --> 00:15:16,295
بَقِيَّتُ اللَّهِ خَيرٌ لَكُم إِن كُنتُم مُؤمِنينَ ۚ

177
00:15:17,348 --> 00:15:24,546
That which is left by Allah for you is better for you; if you are believers, and I'm not set over you as a guardian.

178
00:15:24,576 --> 00:15:29,080
I'm not the Guardian over you; you are responsible for your own dealings and transactions.

179
00:15:29,879 --> 00:15:31,349
What did the people of Shoaib(شُعَيب) say?

180
00:15:31,379 --> 00:15:39,810
And this is you will find something similar in this and what the people would say today when you discuss such an issue with them.

181
00:15:39,935 --> 00:15:54,170
قالوا يا شُعَيبُ أَصَلاتُكَ تَأمُرُكَ أَن نَترُكَ ما يَعبُدُ آباؤُنا أَو أَن نَفعَلَ في أَموالِنا ما نَشاءُ ۖ

182
00:15:54,519 --> 00:15:58,654
إِنَّكَ لَأَنتَ الحَليمُ الرَّشيدُ۝

183
00:15:58,698 --> 00:15:59,422
They said;

184
00:15:59,827 --> 00:16:07,699
O Shoaib(شُعَيب) does your prayer command that we leave off what our fathers used to worship,

185
00:16:07,872 --> 00:16:12,475
or that we leave off doing, what we like to do with our money.

186
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:19,565
They're stating two things in this response.

187
00:16:20,636 --> 00:16:22,554
First of all, they're saying, O Shoaib(شُعَيب);

188
00:16:22,729 --> 00:16:25,229
Your Salah(صلاة), they're talking about the Salah(صلاة) of Shoaib(شُعَيب)

189
00:16:25,975 --> 00:16:34,400
they are telling Syedina(سَيِّدِنَا) Shoaib عليه السلام what does prayer have to do with the religion of our fathers

190
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:38,761
and what does prayer have to do with business?

191
00:16:40,173 --> 00:16:41,952
The explanation of this is;

192
00:16:42,174 --> 00:16:45,943
Number one, what does Salah(صلاة) have to do with the religion of our fathers?

193
00:16:47,617 --> 00:16:54,950
In fact, they to be specific, they said: Does your prayer command that we leave off what our fathers used to worship?

194
00:16:55,436 --> 00:17:00,624
They’re telling Shoaib(شُعَيب), go and pray in your room or in your office and close your office.

195
00:17:01,172 --> 00:17:03,536
What does your prayer have to do with our religion?

196
00:17:04,188 --> 00:17:07,990
Why do you pray and then come and tell us don't worship the religion of our fathers?

197
00:17:08,052 --> 00:17:09,999
What does your prayer have to do with this?

198
00:17:10,091 --> 00:17:14,355
You have your religion, we have ours; your Salah(صلاة) should not involve in this.

199
00:17:14,813 --> 00:17:19,265
They want to separate between the religion of Shoaib(شُعَيب) and their religion.

200
00:17:20,653 --> 00:17:25,716
So they're telling him, to stay and do whatever you want in your religion, but don't bother us.

201
00:17:26,102 --> 00:17:27,946
Don't come and tell us that we're wrong?

202
00:17:28,769 --> 00:17:32,174
What does Salah(صلاة) have to do with the religion of our fathers?

203
00:17:33,459 --> 00:17:37,880
In your Salah(صلاة), your Salah(صلاة) is telling you that we should give up our religion?

204
00:17:38,730 --> 00:17:43,611
And we find this similar in the response given by the Non-believers.

205
00:17:44,242 --> 00:17:51,968
They would say that, keep your religion but don't try to propagate it on us and don't tell us about your religion.

206
00:17:51,998 --> 00:17:56,164
 You keep your religion and we'll keep ours and we'll be friends and we'll get along.

207
00:17:56,590 --> 00:18:02,128
Now on the religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى we have to give out the message of Risala(رسالة), the message of Islam.

208
00:18:03,104 --> 00:18:08,390
The second thing that they stated, they said what does your Salah(صلاة) have to do with business?

209
00:18:10,584 --> 00:18:12,811
What does your Salah(صلاة) have to do with business?

210
00:18:12,871 --> 00:18:14,573
What do we call this today?

211
00:18:16,152 --> 00:18:17,938
What do we call this concept today?

212
00:18:18,073 --> 00:18:18,873
Secularism;

213
00:18:19,343 --> 00:18:20,644
This is secularism;

214
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:26,216
separation between the religion and the aspects of life.

215
00:18:28,031 --> 00:18:32,450
They said: Your Salah(صلاة), this is a ritual this is Ibadah(عبادة), what does it have to do with business?

216
00:18:33,243 --> 00:18:36,690
This is a worship between you and your God

217
00:18:36,952 --> 00:18:40,627
but this business is something that has to do with this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and this world.

218
00:18:40,937 --> 00:18:43,123
We should separate between the two things

219
00:18:43,464 --> 00:18:47,146
leave what is for God for God and what is for Caesar for Caesar.

220
00:18:48,181 --> 00:18:52,483
So, the concept of secularism is not new that people of Shoaib(شُعَيب) knew it a long time ago,

221
00:18:52,674 --> 00:18:59,718
and the Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) of today, the ignorance of today is not any different than the ignorance, a few 1000 years ago.

222
00:18:59,954 --> 00:19:00,986
It's is the same thing.

223
00:19:01,795 --> 00:19:06,274
So, they said that your Salah(صلاة) shouldn't tell us what to do in our business.

224
00:19:06,809 --> 00:19:14,119
This is up to us and that is the problem with mankind when they don't want to follow the law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

225
00:19:14,365 --> 00:19:20,108
The law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is not something that you keep in the Masjid(مسجد), or you keep as an individual,

226
00:19:20,243 --> 00:19:24,798
the law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى applies to every aspect of our life.

227
00:19:25,611 --> 00:19:29,478
All our lives should fall within the Hukum(حكم) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

228
00:19:29,907 --> 00:19:35,215
The religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى controls everything in our livelihood; in the day and in the night

229
00:19:35,477 --> 00:19:43,516
whether it is politics, or it is economics or trade or banking, these other aspects of economics,

230
00:19:43,691 --> 00:19:50,796
whether it is the civil law, whether it is the social relations, whether it is international law and the relations between nations,

231
00:19:51,034 --> 00:19:53,376
the religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى controls all of this.

232
00:19:53,677 --> 00:20:03,004
Now we're living at a time when there is an attempt to separate between the religion of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and all of these aspects

233
00:20:03,488 --> 00:20:13,636
and to turn it into an issue of individual application inside that has no presentation in the outside

234
00:20:13,898 --> 00:20:17,001
that has no manifestation in our actual life.

235
00:20:18,325 --> 00:20:23,109
So if you want to keep your religion between you and yourself, that's fine

236
00:20:23,489 --> 00:20:29,450
but if you want to apply the religion and it's gonna affect the people around you and affect your family and affect the society,

237
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:31,182
No; that's unacceptable

238
00:20:32,769 --> 00:20:34,053
 and that is secularism

239
00:20:34,696 --> 00:20:37,100
and that is what Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) tried to fight.

240
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:44,043
Syedina(سَيِّدِنَا) Shoaib عليه السلام insisted on these points and kept on making Da'wah(دعوة) to them

241
00:20:45,471 --> 00:20:50,360
because they didn't want to understand what he's saying and they didn't attempt to learn it.

242
00:20:50,487 --> 00:20:51,164
They said;

243
00:20:51,188 --> 00:21:00,045
قالوا يا شُعَيبُ ما نَفقَهُ كَثيرًا مِمّا تَقولُ وَإِنّا لَنَراكَ فينا ضَعيفًا ۖ

244
00:21:00,075 --> 00:21:04,632
O Shoaib(شُعَيب)! We do not understand a lot of what you're saying, we don't understand.

245
00:21:05,092 --> 00:21:07,601
This is not because Shoaib(شُعَيب) wasn't clear.

246
00:21:07,998 --> 00:21:13,077
Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) was Khateeb Ul-Ambiyaa(خطيب الأنبِيَاء), he was the Speaker of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), the prophets.

247
00:21:13,246 --> 00:21:15,909
He was very clear and very eloquent

248
00:21:16,544 --> 00:21:22,100
and he would drive the information to them as clear as possible

249
00:21:22,908 --> 00:21:25,779
but they didn't want to understand so they didn't understand.

250
00:21:26,369 --> 00:21:29,811
They did not want to because they were shutting their ears.

251
00:21:31,336 --> 00:21:33,080
They said; We don't understand what you're saying.

252
00:21:33,699 --> 00:21:34,224
And then they said;

253
00:21:34,248 --> 00:21:36,072
وَإِنّا لَنَراكَ فينا ضَعيفًا ۖ

254
00:21:36,310 --> 00:21:39,201
And we see you as a weak man.

255
00:21:39,304 --> 00:21:41,265
They only understand the language of force.

256
00:21:41,692 --> 00:21:42,773
You're weak man.

257
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,544
وَإِنّا لَنَراكَ فينا ضَعيفًا ۖ

258
00:21:44,732 --> 00:21:46,885
 We see you as weak, Daef(ضعيف)

259
00:21:48,711 --> 00:21:56,160
and the only reason, they're not getting rid of him, by killing him is;

260
00:21:56,511 --> 00:22:06,106
وَإِنّا لَنَراكَ فينا ضَعيفًا ۖ وَلَولا رَهطُكَ لَرَجَمناكَ ۖ وَما أَنتَ عَلَينا بِعَزيزٍ۝

261
00:22:06,136 --> 00:22:13,040
Were it not or for your family, we should certainly have stoned you and you are not powerful against us.

262
00:22:14,415 --> 00:22:17,534
Shoaib عليه السّلام was from a noble strong family.

263
00:22:18,205 --> 00:22:18,708
Why?

264
00:22:18,738 --> 00:22:20,893
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

265
00:22:22,139 --> 00:22:27,670
After Saydina Lut(سيدنالوط), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has sent every messenger in a strong family.

266
00:22:28,888 --> 00:22:33,466
We talked about Lut(لوط) last night when he said: I wish that I could lean on a source of power

267
00:22:33,696 --> 00:22:36,973
because Saydina Lut(سيدنالوط) didn't have any family members with him.

268
00:22:37,116 --> 00:22:38,465
He was alone in Sadum(سدوم).

269
00:22:38,751 --> 00:22:40,073
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

270
00:22:40,335 --> 00:22:43,454
أما بعث الله النبي بعد لوط إلَّا في منعتٍ مِن قومه

271
00:22:43,759 --> 00:22:48,894
Any prophet that was sent after Lut(لوط) was sent in a strong family.

272
00:22:50,124 --> 00:22:52,645
So Shoaib(شُعَيب) was sent in a strong family.

273
00:22:52,923 --> 00:22:54,312
So, the people of Shoaib(شُعَيب) are saying;

274
00:22:54,342 --> 00:22:59,660
 If it wasn't for your family, we would kill you and stone you and get rid of you and you can't do anything.

275
00:23:00,139 --> 00:23:06,025
We have no respect for you as an individual and if it's not for the sake of your family, we would kill you.

276
00:23:06,761 --> 00:23:10,677
The message is clear, we don't respect you, you're worthless in our eyes.

277
00:23:10,871 --> 00:23:14,520
It's only for the sake of your family that we're sparing your life.

278
00:23:16,043 --> 00:23:19,357
Look at the response of Syedina(سَيِّدِنَا) Shoaib عليه السلام.

279
00:23:19,413 --> 00:23:20,108
He said;

280
00:23:20,345 --> 00:23:29,174
قالَ يا قَومِ أَرَهطي أَعَزُّ عَلَيكُم مِنَ اللَّهِ وَاتَّخَذتُموهُ وَراءَكُم ظِهرِيًّا ۖ

281
00:23:29,204 --> 00:23:34,075
O my people, is my family have more weight to you than Allah?

282
00:23:35,384 --> 00:23:38,129
You say that you don't want to kill me for my family?

283
00:23:38,836 --> 00:23:42,363
 Allahسُبحانه وتعالى you're not afraid of Him at all?

284
00:23:43,077 --> 00:23:46,514
So you're keeping me alive not for the sake of Allah just because of my family.

285
00:23:46,544 --> 00:23:50,120
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى you're not including him in the equation at all.

286
00:23:50,661 --> 00:23:54,585
He's telling them why should you respect me for my family, respect me for Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

287
00:23:54,646 --> 00:23:55,622
Fear Allah.

288
00:23:56,392 --> 00:23:58,635
وَاتَّخَذتُموهُ وَراءَكُم ظِهرِيًّا ۖ

289
00:23:58,865 --> 00:24:02,079
And you have cast Allah away behind your backs.

290
00:24:02,651 --> 00:24:05,206
They have put Allahسُبحانه وتعالى behind their backs,

291
00:24:05,269 --> 00:24:09,770
they're completely ignoring the law of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى completely

292
00:24:11,727 --> 00:24:18,688
and this is expected from people, who are wealthy and rich and strong.

293
00:24:19,108 --> 00:24:20,849
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

294
00:24:21,102 --> 00:24:22,452
أو غنن متغيَّ

295
00:24:22,773 --> 00:24:25,618
Wealth that will make you arrogant.

296
00:24:26,499 --> 00:24:30,069
When people have money, they feel that they could get everything they want.

297
00:24:30,538 --> 00:24:32,077
They could buy everything.

298
00:24:32,316 --> 00:24:34,491
They could buy material goods,

299
00:24:34,642 --> 00:24:36,118
they can buy happiness,

300
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:37,695
they can buy power,

301
00:24:37,826 --> 00:24:39,164
they can buy fame,

302
00:24:39,196 --> 00:24:41,422
they can buy political positions,

303
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:44,715
people think they can buy anything they want with their money.

304
00:24:45,486 --> 00:24:49,691
A person could start thinking that with my money, I don't need anyone

305
00:24:51,096 --> 00:24:53,243
because I can buy everything with my money,

306
00:24:53,711 --> 00:24:57,561
I don't even need Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, sometimes that happens,

307
00:24:58,439 --> 00:25:00,604
 and the people of Shoaib(شُعَيب) were in that state.

308
00:25:01,086 --> 00:25:06,468
They felt that they don't need anybody, they don't need anyone, they don't even need Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

309
00:25:06,833 --> 00:25:08,167
so they were so arrogant.

310
00:25:10,492 --> 00:25:14,108
They have put Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and the commandments of Allah behind their backs.

311
00:25:14,592 --> 00:25:16,187
So, this is the message of Shoaib(شُعَيب).

312
00:25:16,649 --> 00:25:21,388
I'll recite to you some of the sayings of Shoaib(شُعَيب) that were mentioned the Qur'an.

313
00:25:21,813 --> 00:25:30,441
In these two Ayaat(آيات) Syedina Shoaib(سَيِّدِنَا شُعَيْب) has six pieces of advice that he's giving everyone.

314
00:25:31,298 --> 00:25:33,005
I'll read the Ayaat(آيات) he said;

315
00:25:33,170 --> 00:25:44,540
قالَ يا قَومِ أَرَأَيتُم إِن كُنتُ عَلىٰ بَيِّنَةٍ مِن رَبّي وَرَزَقَني مِنهُ رِزقًا حَسَنًا ۚ

316
00:25:44,794 --> 00:25:51,920
وَما أُريدُ أَن أُخالِفَكُم إِلىٰ ما أَنهاكُم عَنهُ ۚ

317
00:25:52,078 --> 00:25:55,194
إِن أُريدُ إِلَّا الإِصلاحَ مَا استَطَعتُ ۚ

318
00:25:55,503 --> 00:26:03,307
وَما تَوفيقي إِلّا بِاللَّهِ ۚ عَلَيهِ تَوَكَّلتُ وَإِلَيهِ أُنيبُ۝

319
00:26:04,130 --> 00:26:15,435
وَيا قَومِ لا يَجرِمَنَّكُم شِقاقي أَن يُصيبَكُم مِثلُ ما أَصابَ قَومَ نوحٍ أَو قَومَ هودٍ أَو قَومَ صالِحٍ ۚ

320
00:26:15,729 --> 00:26:20,375
وَما قَومُ لوطٍ مِنكُم بِبَعيدٍ۝

321
00:26:20,669 --> 00:26:25,730
وَاستَغفِروا رَبَّكُم ثُمَّ توبوا إِلَيهِ ۚ

322
00:26:26,031 --> 00:26:30,015
إِنَّ رَبّي رَحيمٌ وَدودٌ۝

323
00:26:30,050 --> 00:26:35,073
Oh my people; Tell me, if I have a clear evidence from my Lord,

324
00:26:35,642 --> 00:26:39,063
and He has given me good sustenance from himself.

325
00:26:40,850 --> 00:26:45,519
I wish not in contradiction to you to do that which I forbid you.

326
00:26:45,988 --> 00:26:50,971
I only desire reform so far as I am able to the best of my power

327
00:26:51,281 --> 00:26:56,529
and my guidance cannot come except from Allah in Him I trust and unto him I repent

328
00:26:56,937 --> 00:27:06,012
and O my people, let not my Shiqaaq(شقاق) cause you to suffer the fate similar to that the people of Nuh(نوح) or Hud(هود) or Saleh(صالح)

329
00:27:06,159 --> 00:27:08,953
and the people of Lut(لوط) are not far from you

330
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:13,378
and ask forgiveness of your Lord and turn unto Him in repentance.

331
00:27:13,438 --> 00:27:15,948
Verily, my Lord is Most Merciful and most loving.

332
00:27:16,458 --> 00:27:19,939
In these three Ayaat(آيات), there are six pieces of advice.

333
00:27:20,129 --> 00:27:21,042
Number one,

334
00:27:21,328 --> 00:27:28,367
وَما أُريدُ أَن أُخالِفَكُم إِلىٰ ما أَنهاكُم عَنهُ ۚ

335
00:27:28,397 --> 00:27:33,025
I wish not in contradiction to you to do that which I forbid you.

336
00:27:34,097 --> 00:27:40,594
Shoaib(شُعَيب) is saying: I do not want to do something that is contradicting my words.

337
00:27:42,022 --> 00:27:44,569
If I say something, I must do it

338
00:27:46,846 --> 00:27:53,698
and that is a very important quality of the believer and the opposite is a quality of the hypocrites.

339
00:27:54,089 --> 00:27:57,504
They say things and they don't act upon them.

340
00:27:58,362 --> 00:28:01,043
And they say things and they do the opposite

341
00:28:02,424 --> 00:28:04,549
and this is a very, very dangerous thing

342
00:28:04,598 --> 00:28:07,240
because Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the authentic Hadith(حديث)

343
00:28:07,961 --> 00:28:18,260
that in hellfire there would be a man who's running around his intestines and he is running around them.

344
00:28:18,800 --> 00:28:22,487
So the people of hellfire will come to him and they would say you have harmed us

345
00:28:23,186 --> 00:28:31,435
and then they would tell him, weren't you in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) telling us to do good and you were preventing us from doing evil?

346
00:28:32,145 --> 00:28:33,091
This man used to do,

347
00:28:33,121 --> 00:28:34,744
أمر بالمعروف ونهي عن المنكر

348
00:28:35,435 --> 00:28:39,322
He used to enjoin the people to the good and he would forbid them from doing evil.

349
00:28:40,032 --> 00:28:41,180
Why was he punished?

350
00:28:41,426 --> 00:28:44,926
He would tell them because I used to tell you to do the good and I won't do it

351
00:28:45,235 --> 00:28:48,120
